    "q-44391": {
      "dom_id": "step-q44391",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "The lines $y=\\frac{8}{5}x+9$ and $y=mx+3$ are parallel. The value of $m=$",
      "worked_solution": "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nBoth lines are in slope-intercept form, so we can pick out the slope of each equation by looking at the $x$-coefficient.\n\n- The slope of the line $y=\\frac{8}{5}x+9$ is $\\frac{8}{5}.$\n\n- The slope of the line $y=mx+3$ is $m.$\n\nBecause the slopes must be the same, we must have $m=\\frac{8}{5}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
